# __NAME__

Rust game scaffolded by game-factory (`__SLUG__`). Cargo workspace:

| Crate | What |
|---|---|
| `crates/engine` | Deterministic, dependency-free engines ported from the factory JS libs: PCG32/FNV/legacy streams (`rng`), `physics` (platformer-physics), `hazard` (hazard-kit), `worldgen` (+ fairness validator), `autopilot`. `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`. |
| `crates/game` | macroquad 2D starter: window, fixed 60 Hz step, one-screen platformer demo. |

`spec/` (copied from the factory) holds the language-neutral engine specs and golden vectors. The engines must keep passing
`crates/engine/tests/vectors.rs`; JS stays the reference. Never edit `spec/vectors/*.json` by hand.

## Gates
```sh
export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/datanapps/cargo-target/__SLUG__   # never /tmp
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy -p engine --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test            # default-members = engine only: offline, fast, runs the vectors
cargo check -p game   # needs the network once to fetch macroquad
```
`FACTORY_SPEC_DIR` overrides where the vectors are found (default: search upward for `spec/vectors/rng.json`).

## Run
```sh
cargo run -p game --release
```
Linux native builds need the usual X11/ALSA dev packages; see the macroquad docs.

## Web build (wasm32-unknown-unknown)
```sh
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo build -p game --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
mkdir -p dist && cp $CARGO_TARGET_DIR/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/game.wasm dist/
```
Serve `dist/` with an `index.html` that loads macroquad's `mq_js_bundle.js` (from the macroquad repo) and calls
`load("game.wasm")` on a `<canvas id="glcanvas">`. Release profile is size-tuned (`opt-level="z"`, LTO, strip,
`panic="abort"`); note `autopilot::trajectory` cannot swallow panics under `panic=abort`.

## Determinism rules
f64 only, integer-only RNG (`engine::rng`), no clock or `rand` inside engine code, fixed-step simulation. Tolerances in vectors:
ints exact, floats 1e-9.
